          "Forest ecologists caution against romanticizing these networks as purely altruistic communities, noting that fungi ultimately prioritize their own survival and resource trade. Even so, the discovery has reshaped sustainable forestry. Clear-cutting entire stands severs fungal webs and slows regrowth, whereas retaining mature 'hub' trees preserves subterranean networks that help young saplings establish more resiliently."
